<title>GERMANY: Pan-German July industry output up 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German July industry output up 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT July 96    June 96    July 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.2	 +0.7	 +1.0</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -1.6	 -0.8	 +2.1</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		98.7	 98.5	100.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				   July 96		  June 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			74.2	-3.0	76.5	-2.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    96.4	-0.3	96.7	+0.9</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   100.0	+0.4	99.6	+1.1</p>
<p>	Capital goods	95.8	+0.3	95.5	+1.3</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  86.9	+0.8	86.2	+2.4</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     94.0	-3.9	97.8	-1.3</p>
<p> Energy output	    106.4	-0.2     106.6	+0.5</p>
<p> Construction	     120.5	+4.2     115.6	-0.8 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 96 with Apr/May 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  +1.0</p>
<p> Construction			    +2.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.0</p>
<p> Mining				    -1.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   +1.5</p>
<p> Consumer durables		     +3.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods			  -2.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +2.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison June/July 1996 with June/July 1995:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -0.7</p>
<p> Mining				    -7.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 unch</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   -1.9</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +2.1</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +3.2</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -1.3</p>
<p> Energy output			   +4.6</p>
<p> Construction			    -6.1</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
